{
  "_comment": [
    "Referents that never become a word at all -- a pack author's hard fence (design 8.4), checked at",
    "derivation rather than at resolution so an unsayable thing is honestly absent instead of silently",
    "dropped. Distinct from `withheld`, a timing fence on things that DO become writable later, and from",
    "`cannot_appear_in_loot`, which keeps a word off found pages and leaves it writable.",
    "",
    "The mod's own stones are NOT here (2026-09-06): deretheni and temperstone are writable and gated by",
    "PRICE instead -- they carry `requires_masterwork_ink`.",
    "",
    "**The algae is a collision rather than a prohibition.** The block and its placed feature share the id",
    "`agesandtheart:algae`, so a derived BLOCK word would claim that name for a material and shadow the",
    "feature -- the one a writer actually wants. Measured: `algae features` resolved to",
    "`surface.material=agesandtheart:algae` and grew nothing. Fencing the block leaves the name meaning the",
    "growth (design 7.6). An Age paved in algae is not a thing to want, and the mat is still placeable.",
    "",
    "**A scarab nest is made by a scarab and nothing else** (design 7.1.2): a written one would stand a",
    "colony's claims in an Age no colony chose. The grazed torchflower is a stage a flower passes through,",
    "and grows back into the flower. A paper tree's heart is the plant itself, grown and never placed: a",
    "written one would stand a tree's claim to the ground where no tree grew."
  ],
